is found, (b) publish anonymous summaries instead, (c) share those
summaries with complainants, and (d) suspend complainants who breach
confidentiality;

6. Amend sections 6.1 and 6.3 to limit complaints to Vancouver residents
and consider requiring a refundable filing fee;

7. Clarify confidentiality rules in sections 6.38–6.40 to strengthen and better
define expectations;

8. Amend the Code to (a) make Council members accountable for Code
breaches by staff they direct and (b) confirm the Integrity Commissioner
has no jurisdiction over political staff – those complaints go to the City;

9. Consider removing Advisory Board Members from the Code’s complaint
and investigation process; and

10. Have staff review and potentially integrate other detailed amendments
listed in the table attached to the report where appropriate.

